/* book Worked example 2: Q: The pump of the first example feeds a six-cylinder four-stroke engine at 1500 rpm with diesel of density 830 kg/m³. Find the fuel per injection in mg and the engine's fuel consumption in kg/h.
   1. Mass per injection = 1.508×10⁻⁷ m³ × 830 kg/m³ = 1.252×10⁻⁴ kg = 125.2 mg.
   2. The pump camshaft turns at 1500 ÷ 2 = 750 rpm, so each element injects 750 times a minute; six elements give 4500 injections a minute.
   3. Fuel = 1.252×10⁻⁴ × 4500 = 0.5632 kg/min = 0.5632 × 60 = 33.8 kg/h.
   Answer: 125.2 mg per injection and about 33.8 kg/h, a full-load figure for a large truck engine. */
