/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Start at the tank.
   - A pressure sensor on the rail reports to the electronic control unit (ECU).
   - Rail pressure is set by the pump output and the pressure control valve.
   - For a fixed nozzle, the volume per injection rises with injector open time and with the square root of the pressure difference across the nozzle, rail pressure minus cylinder pressure:
   - Q = Cd A t √(2 (prail − pcyl) ÷ ρ) Q is the fuel volume per injection (m³); CdA is the effective hole area (m²); t is the open time (s); prail and pcyl are in Pa; ρ is the diesel density (kg/m³).
   - The ECU can split one injection into several pulses.
   - The system is flexible but not free.
*/
