/* book Worked example 2: Q: At 1200 bar rail pressure and 60 bar cylinder pressure, an injector open for 1.0 ms delivers 30 mm³. The ECU raises the rail to 1800 bar for a finer spray. What open time gives the same 30 mm³? Treat CdA as constant and neglect the needle's opening and closing.
   1. Q = CdA t √(2Δp ÷ ρ), so for the same Q, t₂ = t₁ √(Δp₁ ÷ Δp₂).
   2. Δp₁ = 1200 − 60 = 1140 bar; Δp₂ = 1800 − 60 = 1740 bar.
   3. t₂ = 1.0 × √(1140 ÷ 1740) = 1.0 × √0.6552 = 1.0 × 0.8094 = 0.809 ms.
   Answer: About 0.81 ms. Leaving the pulse at 1.0 ms would give 30 × √(1740 ÷ 1140) = 37.1 mm³, a 24 % overdose, which is why the ECU always reads rail pressure. */
