/* book exam traps: Saying rail pressure alone sets injection quantity. Quantity depends on rail pressure and injector open time together (Q ∝ t√Δp). | Treating common rail as a petrol-only system. This chapter is diesel common rail; petrol direct injection uses a similar rail but different mixture needs. | Thinking pilot injection adds power. The pilot pulse mainly shortens the delay of the main charge and cuts noise; the main pulse's fuel gives the work. | Calling post injection a late power pulse only. Its main job is exhaust after-treatment, such as diesel particulate filter regeneration. | Assuming higher rail pressure is always better. It improves spray but raises pump work, nitrogen oxides and wear, so the ECU balances it. */
